Yes, there are advantages to having a powerful pet who kills
everything.  Thvor has roughly 10,000 Zorkmids she otherwise wouldn't
have, and could go back to minetown for even more.  But just because
something has many advantages does not mean that it's not a bug; I've
seen many games get patched to remove an overly advantageous
item/ability/whatever (commonly referred to as "nerfing").  I felt
(and still feel) that, for neutral & lawful characters at least,
having pets running amuck (and killing otherwise unkillable
shopkeepers and priests) was inappropriate (and therefore a bug).  I
posted here looking to see if someone else had already written a patch
for this, in order to save myself some work, or to get advice on
where/how to implement the patch, since I'd not worked on the NH
source yet.  I have since implemented it, and am currently testing to
make sure I've got it right.

As for your comment about cursed items not behaving as one would
expect: actually, I find that they do.  Cursed means the opposite of
blessed, and thus a cursed item should not be helpful (or at least,
not very helpful).  Cursed scrolls of enchant armor actually
de-enchant armor.  Makes sense to me.  Something useful has been
warped and turned against its original purpose, as expected.  I don't
see how this has any relation to pets killing wantonly and their
owners not being held responsible for it.

